  nonce: c5cd  # c5cd
  message: "I concur with this. We just need to have good docstrings."  # c5cd
- op: update  # 9478
  at: '2026-04-27T15:13:21Z'  # 9478
  by: agent  # 9478
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 9478
  clock: 8  # 9478
  nonce: '9478'  # 9478
  set:  # 9478
    description: "Add a minimal but useful tag management / organization layer to `scripts/tracker`. The trigger is enumeration (so the existing-coverage check at structural-fix-scope-expansion-protocol.md §\"When NOT to file a new tracker item\" point 1 can actually run), but the same mechanic exposes catalog metadata (description, timestamps) and lifecycle verbs (rename / describe / deprecate) that keep the tag namespace coherent over time.\n\n**Motivating gap (jgstern, WI-mobup 2026-04-27T14:17:40Z + 14:33Z):** the playbook's spot-check step tells the agent to run `scripts/tracker list --tag <plausible-tag>`. That assumes the agent already knows which tags exist — but `scripts/tracker` has no enumeration command. `--tag` only filters by an *already-known* value. Layered on top: with no rename / describe / deprecate story, near-duplicates accumulate (`developer_experience` vs `dx`, `bakeoff_infrastructure` vs `bakeoff_infra`) and silently dilute filterability over time.\n\n---\n\n## Locked design (concurred 2026-04-27)\n\n### Status model — three external states from two underlying values\n\n| Stored: `deprecated` flag | Observed: `count` of items with this tag | External `status` |\n|---|---|---|\n| false | > 0 | **active**     |\n| false | == 0 | **inactive**   |\n| true  | (any) | **deprecated** |\n\n`active` = current uses, no opinion.\n`inactive` = no current uses, no explicit retirement decision; re-using is fine.\n`deprecated` = explicit retirement decision; `tracker add --tag <deprecated>` should warn (and surface the canonical replacement recorded in `in_favor_of` when present). Independent of count, so a tag deprecated *while* still affixed to live items keeps firing the warning on new uses while existing usages stay untouched until cleanup.\n\nThis mirrors the tracker's existing `deprecated_statuses` precedent (`config.yaml` per-kind list, see `validation.py:295` and AGENTS.md note 'Do NOT use `holding` — it is deprecated') — same word, same lifecycle semantics, applied to tag names instead of status names.\n\n### Catalog file: `.agent/tracker/tag_catalog.yaml` (sibling of `config.yaml`)\n\n```yaml\ntags:\n  developer_experience:\n    description: 'Things that make agent / human developer life better.'\n    created_on: 2026-01-15T10:30:00Z\n    last_modified: 2026-04-20T14:00:00Z   # name / description / deprecated changes\n    last_used: 2026-04-27T14:50:00Z       # last add or remove on any item\n    deprecated: false\n    in_favor_of: null                     # optional canonical replacement when deprecated\n```\n\n`status` is **not** a stored field. It is computed at read time from `(count_of_items_with_tag, deprecated)`.\n\n### Stored vs derived\n\n| Field | Storage |\n|---|---|\n| `description` | stored on catalog entry |\n| `created_on` | stored on catalog entry; first-time backfill walks the op log |\n| `last_modified` | stored on catalog entry; updated on rename / describe / deprecate |\n| `last_used` | stored on catalog entry; updated on every `add` / `update` that touches an item's tag list |\n| `deprecated` | stored on catalog entry |\n| `in_favor_of` | stored on catalog entry (optional) |\n| `count` | derived (one pass over compiled tier index — same cost as `tags --count` already pays) |\n| `status` | derived (`{count, deprecated}` → 3-way) |\n\n### Subcommand surface\n\n| Form | Behavior |\n|---|---|\n| `tracker tags` | List every tag in use, sorted alphabetically, one per line. |\n| `tracker tags --count` | `tag<TAB>count<TAB>status` rows, sorted by count desc then alpha. |\n| `tracker tags --json` | `{ \"<tag>\": { \"count\": N, \"status\": \"...\", \"description\": \"...\", \"created_on\": \"...\", \"last_modified\": \"...\", \"last_used\": \"...\", \"deprecated\": bool, \"in_favor_of\": null|\"<tag>\" } }`. |\n| `tracker tags rename OLD NEW` | Rewrite every item's `tags` list, replacing OLD with NEW. Idempotent. De-dupes when both already exist on the same item. Updates catalog `last_modified` on both entries. |\n| `tracker tags describe TAG [TEXT]` | Set / read the description. With no TEXT, prints current description (or empty). Updates catalog `last_modified`. |\n| `tracker tags deprecate TAG [--in-favor-of NEW]` | Set the deprecated flag. Optional `--in-favor-of` records the canonical replacement; future `tracker add --tag <deprecated>` emits a warning that mentions it. Updates catalog `last_modified`. |\n\n**Stretch (file as child item if main lift is bigger than expected):**\n- `tracker tags merge OLD INTO_NEW` — alias of `rename` with audit-trail-friendly verb.\n- `tracker add --tag <deprecated>` warning hook (touches the existing `add` codepath, not the new subcommand).\n\n**Out of scope:**\n- Tag hierarchies.\n- Filter-time aliases (`--tag dx` matching `developer_experience`).\n- Per-tier tag visibility.\n\n### Op-log backfill on first invocation\n\nOn first `tracker tags` invocation after this lands, scan the op log to populate `created_on` (earliest op that introduced the tag on any item) and `last_used` (latest op that added or removed the tag on any item) for every tag currently in use. Write the catalog file. Subsequent invocations see the catalog already present and skip the backfill. Migration cost is paid once.\n\n### Tier handling\n\nRead-only enumeration over canonical ∪ workspace by default (matches the CI-visible set). Add `--tier stealth` later if needed. Stealth-tier-only tags are not enumerated by default.\n\n### Docstring requirements (per AGENTS.md \"Module Docstrings\")\n\nEvery module / function this PR adds must have a substantive docstring explaining **how it works and why**, not just **what it exports**:\n\n- The new `tags` subcommand module's top-level docstring should name the three-state model, point to the catalog schema, explain why `status` is derived rather than stored (smaller bug surface, no sync requirement on `rename` / `add` / `update` paths), and reference this tracker item.\n- The catalog read/write helpers should document the YAML schema inline, name the invariants (e.g. \"every key in `tags:` matches `^[a-z_][a-z0-9_]*$`\", \"`in_favor_of` only meaningful when `deprecated` is true\"), and explain the op-log backfill trigger condition.\n- The hooks into `add` / `update` that maintain `last_used` should document the failure mode they're guarding against (\"if we don't update last_used here, the catalog drifts from reality silently and the inactive-vs-active classification becomes meaningless\").\n- The deprecation warning hook in `tracker add --tag <name>` should document why warnings (not blocks) — the `holding` precedent established that deprecated values stay readable; the same applies to writes during a migration window.\n\n### Tests\n\n- Empty corpus → `tags` prints nothing, exit 0.\n- Corpus with 3 items having tags `[a, b]` / `[b, c]` / `[a]` → `a\\nb\\nc\\n` (sorted) for `tags`; `[(\"a\",2,\"active\"),(\"b\",2,\"active\"),(\"c\",1,\"active\")]` for `--count`.\n- After `tracker tags rename a x` on the above → `a` is `inactive` (count 0), `x` is `active` (count 2). Idempotent on re-run.\n- `tracker tags describe foo \"purpose\"` round-trips via `tracker tags describe foo`.\n- `tracker tags deprecate foo --in-favor-of bar` flips `deprecated=true`; subsequent `tracker add --tag foo` emits a warning mentioning `bar` to stderr (does not block the add).\n- Op-log backfill: corpus with item created at T1 with tag `x`, item updated at T2 to add tag `y`, no tag_catalog.yaml present → first `tracker tags` invocation populates catalog with `x.created_on=T1`, `x.last_used=T1`, `y.created_on=T2`, `y.last_used=T2`.\n- Tier filter: stealth-only items excluded from default enumeration; appear under `--tier stealth`.\n\n### Cross-references\n\n- WI-mobup-matih-folit-maraj-zigid-zopab-bibat-vokak — re-opened pending this; isbefore edge points there.\n- `.agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/structural-fix-scope-expansion-protocol.md` §\"When NOT to file a new tracker item\" point 1 (the call-site that this enables).\n- `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py` — where the new subcommand lands.\n- `.agent/tracker/tag_catalog.yaml` — new sibling file; schema documented above.\n- `validation.py:295` — `deprecated_statuses` precedent for the deprecation lifecycle vocabulary."  # 9478
